t/m/4671872220764/images/template/default/profile/profile_default_m.jpg" class="lite-image" alt="Daniel Atzberger"></picture></span><span class="nova-legacy-v-person-inline-item__fullname">Daniel Atzberger</span></span></a></li><li class="nova-legacy-e-list__item"><a class="nova-legacy-e-link nova-legacy-e-link--color-inherit nova-legacy-e-link--theme-bare" href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Toshiko-Matsui-2" type="button"><span class="nova-legacy-v-person-inline-item"><span class="lite-person-inline-item__image"><picture class="lite-page-avatar lite-page-avatar--size-xs lite-page-avatar--radius-full"> <img src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mN89OjNfwAJDwOxHEacwgAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==" data-src="https://i1.rgstatic.net/ii/profile.image/708876030713856-1546020624601_Q64/Toshiko-Matsui-2.jpg" class="lite-image" alt="Toshiko Matsui"></picture></span><span class="nova-legacy-v-person-inline-item__fullname">Toshiko Matsui</span></span></a></li><li class="nova-legacy-e-list__item"><a class="nova-legacy-e-link nova-legacy-e-link--color-inherit nova-legacy-e-link--theme-bare" href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Robert-Henker-3" type="button"><span class="nova-legacy-v-person-inline-item"><span class="lite-person-inline-item__image"><picture class="lite-page-avatar lite-page-avatar--size-xs lite-page-avatar--radius-full"> <img src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mN89OjNfwAJDwOxHEacwgAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==" data-src="https://i1.rgstatic.net/ii/profile.image/11431281173634760-1688996535980_Q64/Robert-Henker-3.jpg" class="lite-image" alt="Robert Henker"></picture></span><span class="nova-legacy-v-person-inline-item__fullname">Robert Henker</span></span></a></li><li class="nova-legacy-e-list__item"><a class="nova-legacy-e-link nova-legacy-e-link--color-inherit nova-legacy-e-link--theme-bare" href="https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/William-Knottenbelt-2222139446" type="button"><span class="nova-legacy-v-person-inline-item"><span class="nova-legacy-v-person-inline-item__fullname">William Knottenbelt</span></span></a></li></ul></div><div class="nova-legacy-v-publication-item__stack-item"><div class="nova-legacy-e-text nova-legacy-e-text--size-m nova-legacy-e-text--family-sans-serif nova-legacy-e-text--spacing-none nova-legacy-e-text--color-inherit nova-legacy-e-text--clamp-3 nova-legacy-v-publication-item__description"><span class="js-target-abstract-69b8efd8ab971 lite-page-hidden">In 2016, BitMEX introduced a novel type of crypto derivates â€“ Perpetual Swaps, i.e., futures with an infinite term. Perpetual swaps provide a new strategic risk management tool for cryptocurrencies due to their custody-free nature, high leverage, and funding mechanism, but there has been little quantitative analysis on the their benefits. In this paper, we introduce a trading strategy that combines a Quanto Perpetual Swap with a spot position to benefit from the funding mechanism. We compare our strategy with a long-only investment in the underlying cryptocurrency and a similar strategy based on Linear Perpetual Swaps to evaluate their performances in a large-scale backtest covering the years 2021 and 2022. Our analysis shows that our strategy generates positive returns in bullish market phases of the underlying with lower volatility.</span></div></div></div></div><div class="nova-legacy-v-publication-item__footer"><div class="nova-legacy-v-publication-item__footer-actions"><div class="nova-legacy-o-pack nova-legacy-o-pack--gutter-m nova-legacy-o-pack--width-auto nova-legacy-o-pack--vertical-align-middle"><div class="nova-legacy-o-pack__item nova-legacy-v-publication-item__footer-button-group"><div class="nova-legacy-c-button-group nova-legacy-c-button-group--gutter-m nova-legacy-c-button-group--orientation-horizontal nova-legacy-c-button-group--width-auto nova-legacy-v-publication-item__actions"><div class="nova-legacy-c-button-group__item"